`testcase.py` creates `Faker("th_TH")`, seeds it, makes four earlier provider calls, and then calls `pricetag()`. In `faker/providers/currency/__init__.py`, `pricetag()` returns the selected fiat currency code, then a no-break space, then `numerify()` applied to one of the `price_formats`. The Thai locale file overrides `currencies` but not `pricetag()`, so the code comes from the Thai currency tuple pool; for this seeded call sequence, the selected code is `CNY`, and the chosen numerified format produces `14,948.22`. Combining them with the required no-break space gives the exact result.

## Answer
{"pricetag":"CNY 14,948.22"}
